DESCRIPTION:Dennis Ray Wright\, age 79\, of Marceline\, Missouri\, passed 
 away Sunday\, August 16\, 2026\, at Pioneer Skilled Nursing in Marceline. 
 Dennis was born on August 5\, 1947\, on the family farm in Chariton County
 \, Missouri\, the son of Carl Warren and Freda Louise (York) Wright. Denni
 s served in the United States Army and was united in marriage to Kathy Wes
 tfall on May 20\, 1967\, at St. Bonaventure Catholic Church in Marceline. 
 Dennis earned his Master’s degree from Missouri State Teachers College i
 n Kirksville\, Missouri. He worked as a guidance counselor at Macon Vo-Tec
 h. Teacher and coach at Marceline. After retiring\, he worked at Bucklin R
 -2 as a counselor. Dennis enjoyed farming\, hunting\, fishing\, and especi
 ally spending time with his family. Dennis is survived by his wife\, Kathy
 \, of Marceline\; three children\, Julie Lucas and her husband Randy\, Tho
 mas Wright\, and Alicen Wright\, all of Marceline\; six grandchildren\, Cl
 ayton\, Blake\, Whitney\, Winston\, Hillary\, and Justin\; seven great-gra
 ndchildren\, Bentley\, Zane\, Sally\, Remi\, Cooper\, Theodor\, and Emmy\;
  two brothers\, Rodney Wright and wife Shirley of Marceline and Lanny Wrig
 ht and wife Brenda of Chillicothe\; and one sister\, Mary James and husban
 d Ed of Calhoun\, Missouri. He was preceded in death by his parents and fo
 ur brothers\, Taylor\, Gerald “Abe\,” Allen\, and Bradly Wright. Arran
 gements are under the direction of Delaney Funeral Home in Marceline.\n\nF
 ull obituary and service details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obitu
 aries/Dennis-Ray-Wright?obId=49298351
